\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Output of \texttt  {python main.py}: one synthetic dataset of ten years, $\lambda =1$, fee of 3 basis points, pruning on. Annualised figures; turnover per week; fees per year. The training columns cover fitting and checking weeks together. One dataset proves nothing: the three test Sharpe ratios differ by less than 0.1, and the standard error of a one-year Sharpe ratio is 1.0. Table~\ref {tab:prune} repeats the comparison on 20 datasets per setting.}}{12}{table.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
